<article class="env-proposition" id="0B62B7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B62B7">Proposition <span data-tag="0B62B7">7.2.1.14</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-topos and let $\tau _{\leq 0} : \calX \rightarrow \tau _{\leq 0} \calX $ denote a left adjoint to the inclusion. A morphism $\phi : U \rightarrow X$ in $\calX $ is an effective epimorphism if and only if $\tau _{\leq 0}(\phi )$ is an effective epimorphism in the ordinary topos $\rm {h} \it {(\tau _{\leq 0} \calX )}$. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Suppose first that $\phi $ is an effective epimorphism. Let $U_{\bullet }: \Nerve \cDelta _{+}^{op} \rightarrow \calX $ be a Čech nerve of $\phi $, so that $U_{\bullet }$ is a colimit diagram. Since $\tau _{\leq 0}$ is a left adjoint, $\tau _{\leq 0} U_{\bullet }$ is a colimit diagram in $\tau _{\leq 0} \calX $. Using Proposition <a href="/tag/5C64D1" data-tag="5C64D1">6.2.3.10</a>, we deduce easily that $\tau _{\leq 0} \phi $ is an effective epimorphism. 
    <p>
      For the converse, choose a factorization of $\phi $ as a composition 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  U \stackrel{\phi '}{\rightarrow } V \stackrel{\phi ''}{\rightarrow } X \]
</div>
    <p>
       where $\phi '$ is an effective epimorphism and $\phi ''$ is a monomorphism. Applying Lemma <a href="/tag/53083B" data-tag="53083B">7.2.1.13</a> to the $\infty $-topos $\calX _{/ \tau _{\leq 0} X}$, we conclude that $\phi ''$ is the pullback of a monomorphism $i: \overline{V} \rightarrow \tau _{\leq 0} X$. Since the effective epimorphism $\tau _{\leq 0}(\phi )$ factors through $i$, we conclude that $i$ is an equivalence, so that $\phi ''$ is likewise an equivalence. It follows that $\phi $ is an effective epimorphism as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>